.SH "Collaboration"
.PP
In an element-centered finite volume computation, the \fBIsoparametricQuadraticTetrahedron\fP collaborates with the QuadraticTriangle element\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Quadratic tetrahedral finite-element with local interpolation function and Jacobian transformation capability\&. The node numbering of the tetrahedron with regard to the local coordinate frame is: 
.PP
.nf
      ^ t
      |
      |

    4 o
      | \\
      |   \\
    8 o     o 10
      |      \\

.fi
.PP
 9 o | \\ 1 o -- o --- o 3 --> s / 7 / 5 o o 6 / / o 2 r

.PP
Note that this numbering scheme is different from that used by ICEMCFD where node 7 (0\&.\&.n-1) is the midside node of the edge 0-3, node 8 of edge 1-3, and node 9 of edge 2-3\&. 
.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticTetrahedron::IsoparametricQuadraticTetrahedron ()"
Default constructor initializes quadratic tetrahedron to use local coordinates and a 4-point integration scheme where the Gauss points are located near the corners\&. 
